    "id": "p5-p2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Let $$f(x)=\\frac{x}{x^2-1}.$$ Show that $$f(x)+f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)=0,$$ where $x\\ne0,\\pm1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f\\left(\\dfrac1x\\right)=-\\dfrac{x}{x^2-1}=-f(x)$, so the sum is $0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=\\frac{1/x}{1/x^2-1}\\\\f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=\\frac{x}{1-x^2}\\\\f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=-\\frac{x}{x^2-1}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)+f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=\\frac{x}{x^2-1}-\\frac{x}{x^2-1}\\\\f(x)+f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
